        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear Colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital stay of your patient, a 54-year-old male, admitted on 07/08/2019 due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Clinical examination, chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, and pulse oximetry confirmed an acute exacerbation. Spirometry supported the diagnosis of severe airflow obstruction. Treatment consisted of nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and supportive measures. The patient responded well to treatment with significant clinical improvement. He was discharged on 08/08/2019 in stable condition. Please arrange follow-up including pulmonary function review and optimisation of maintenance inhaler therapy. Should you have any questions, please do not hesitate to contact me. Yours sincerely, Dr. [Treating Physician]</div>"
            },
